cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Mutation Score Understates Oracle Provenance: Agent-Generated Test
  Suites on Defects4J, With and Without the Implementation
message: >-
  If you use this data or these scripts, please cite the repository.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Parpal
    given-names: Sergi
repository-code: https://github.com/sergiparpal/mutation-study
abstract: >-
  Two test suites were generated per Defects4J bug with the same agent and
  model, under two conditions: the agent either works inside the checked-out
  project or sees only its javadoc. Over 36 bugs measured in both arms,
  real-fault detection falls from 72% to 14%, while mutation score falls from
  58% to 44% and line coverage from 85% to 73%. With an EvoSuite baseline over
  the same subjects, EvoSuite and the specification-only suites are nearly
  tied on mutation score and differ nearly three-fold in detection. The
  repository holds the generation and measurement scripts, the per-suite
  measurements, a hand classification of the 40 faults, a probe of what the
  model recalls about each fault with no code in context, two post-cutoff
  replication corpora, and an audit of what the benchmark's own files told
  the agent.
keywords:
  - test generation
  - mutation testing
  - Defects4J
  - large language models
  - empirical software engineering
license: MIT
license-url: https://github.com/sergiparpal/mutation-study/blob/main/LICENSE
date-released: 2026-10-01
